#  SovereignOS Kernel Panic Handler
#  File: kernel_panic_handler.support
#===============================================================================
#  PURPOSE:
#    Engineering reference for the SovereignOS panic handler responsible for:
#      • panic event capture
#      • stack trace extraction
#      • crash signature generation
#      • safe-mode escalation
#      • persistent panic logging
#
#===============================================================================
#  MODULE SUMMARY:
#
#    - [Panic Capture](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Panic_Capture)
#    - [Stack Trace](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Stack_Trace)
#    - [Crash Signatures](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Crash_Signatures)
#    - [Safe Mode](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Safe_Mode)
#    - [Panic Snapshot](ca://s?q=Explain_Kernel_Panic_Snapshot)
#
#===============================================================================
#  FUNCTION OVERVIEW:
#
#    - panic(subsystem, message, meta)
#         Captures panic event.
#
#    - clear()
#         Clears panic + exits safe mode.
#
#    - last()
#         Returns last panic entry.
#
#    - snapshot()
#         Returns panic handler state.
#
#===============================================================================
#  PANIC ENTRY FORMAT:
#
#    {
#      "id": "PNC-XXXX",
#      "subsystem": "scheduler",
#      "message": "null pointer",
#      "meta": { ... },
#      "stack": [ ... ],
#      "signature": "<crash-hash>",
#      "timestamp": <epoch>
#    }
#
